-- Descriptions only: tidy the tables' and functions' descriptions after the changes of 20–26 Oct (document audit,
-- 26 Oct 2026). No behaviour changes: only `comment on` statements.
--   - markets and markets.layout: the layout no longer decides the cabin (by distance since 26 Oct, manual §5), and
--     Reference → Markets has no layout box since #105.
--   - aircraft.checked_on and schedule_changed_on: the one-week check went on 22 Oct; kept, read by nothing.
--   - growth_signals(), airline_cards() and cash_log(): the screens that read them since 20 Oct (Check and Review went).
--   - order_cabin(): the planner doesn't call it; filing takes the plan card's cabin, else the aircraft's order_config_id.

comment on table public.markets is 'Each airline''s markets. Since 21 Oct a market keeps only its layout: its default aircraft, default cabin and fares went (spec docs/specs/2026-10-21-cabins-new-rule.md). Since 26 Oct the layout is kept but no longer decides the cabin (manual §5: the cabin by distance). Replaces the planner''s ref.markets.';

comment on column public.markets.layout is 'Since 26 Oct no longer read by the cabin rule (manual §5: the cabin by distance). Was: the cabin layout the market calls for (Standard, Leisure, Leisure Plus or Comfort), taken by a plan card where one route of the market flew more than cabin_route_share_pct of the aircraft''s block time. Kept as history; no longer shown or changed in Reference → Markets (#105)';

comment on column public.aircraft.checked_on is 'Was the one-week check, Gitesh''s to mark; the check went on 22 Oct (manual §1). Kept, read by nothing (filing clears it)';

comment on column public.aircraft.schedule_changed_on is 'Was when its schedule last changed, which restarted the one-week check; the check went on 22 Oct. Kept, read by nothing (filing clears it)';

comment on function public.growth_signals(bigint, timestamp with time zone) is 'Performance''s growth signals and Today''s routes to fix, across our airlines in a world (the default world when null; decision #19, design §8; the old planner''s capSignalsHtml and patterns): from route_profit() and aircraft_profit() over growth_window_days, ready for another flight (mark add, by profit a week), raise fares (by flights), fix or reduce (losing or fix, by profit a flight) and aircraft losing money after their lease (by net); and the load patterns: each route''s departures over the load window (load_window_days, ending two days ahead, leaving out each rotation''s first load_leeway_days) by load band, marked cut, watch, add or hold from the pattern_* settings. profit_captured: whether any bank-statement line was posted since midnight UTC 8 days before p_as_of (the old Home lists the routes the load patterns mark cut when none was). Staff only; runs as owner and checks the caller itself.';

comment on function public.airline_cards(bigint, timestamp with time zone) is 'Performance''s scorecards and Today''s orders: a card for each of our active airlines in a world (the default world when null), in display order (decision #19, design §8; the old planner''s finStats, renderFinance and fcNext): profit a day over the last 7 days of reported cash (an early read over fewer, early true), per aircraft, return on fleet a week, an aircraft pays back in and funds a new aircraft every (days), fleet, on order, flights a day and how many more than a week ago, average load over 7 days, next_order and can_order_now (cash_forecast()); and group_today (groupOverviewHtml): per airline cash, flight profit a day, this week''s leases and week-end closing per day (each, and together), net, and aircraft arrived but not yet flying with their leases a day (group_today_shown once any airline has flight profit). No group totals (manual §1). Money in millions of AS$. And the group''s average economy load over 7 days, the old Home''s key figure (avgLF): load_7_days, the average of every flight the loads pages captured departing from 7 days before p_as_of''s UTC date on (one per airline, date and flight number), with load_7_days_flights and load_7_days_from captures; with none captured, every flight the last 7 days'' load reports cover (route_loads()), from reports; with neither, null. Staff only; runs as owner and checks the caller itself.';

comment on function public.cash_log(bigint, timestamp with time zone) is 'Systems → Manual entry''s nightly log and its cash entry form for our active airlines in a world (the default world when null), in display order (#18 build pull request 10; the old planner''s finSeries, applyCaptureCash and cashEntryHtml): per airline each reported date (airline_profit()''s, the first included) with its cash and its fixed costs for the next 7 days as the old planner shows them (for a capture day in the 7 days to p_as_of''s UTC date, the events'' payments in the 7 days after that day''s latest balance, when there are any; otherwise a typed figure, else the capture''s, above zero only); and for today (p_as_of''s UTC date) the figures a typed one is saved against: shown (the form''s), stored (what the tables give the old planner: a typed figure, else the capture''s rounded to 0.01M), captured (capture_cash rounded) and the typed row (cash_entries: cash and fixed_next7 in AS$, updated_at) when there is one. Money in millions of AS$ unless named. Staff only; runs as owner and checks the caller itself.';

comment on function public.order_cabin(bigint, bigint) is 'The cabin layout an order of a type comes with for an airline (decision #18, build pull request 7; private.fig_order_cabin(), since 15 Oct the data Reference changes: the airline''s own in airline_order_cabins, else the type''s aircraft_types.order_config_id, filled from the old planner''s DEFAULT_CABIN): {id, code, cabin, cost, aircraft_type_id}, or null when there is none. The planner doesn''t call it: filing takes the plan card''s cabin, else the aircraft''s order_config_id. Staff only; runs as owner and checks the caller itself.';
